{
  "_why": "Role track for FOUNDRY / FORGING, a new trade (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #11, sheet 19). fam_foundry_forging binds the casting and forging NCO codes at job-domain specificity 50: the 7211 moulders and core makers (not 7211.0101/.0102, the press shop's), the 8121 casting codes (helper, assistant technician, die casting, PDC, non-ferrous casting, machine core maker), the 7221 forging codes (power hammer, forging operator, hammer man, stamper) and 7223.0300 drop-forging setter, plus the four casting / forging shop supervisor codes (3122.4401/.4402/.4501/.4502: a trade supervisor keeps his trade, sheet 23). Village blacksmiths (7221.0100/.0200) stay on fam_blacksmithing.",
  "_scope": "THE CASTING AND FORGING SHOP. Melting, moulding, core making, die casting, pouring and fettling, and hammer / press / upset forging and trimming. Heat treatment of the finished part is the Heat-Treatment trade (sheet 17); machining it is the machinist's.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS foundry_experience, asked FIRST. Its options carry value_number ONLY: pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, and a value_text would turn every gte below into a string compare that is false forever (the #776 defect).",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Easy is 2 trade items + at most 1 confirm; Medium adds 2 (process, material); Advanced adds 2 (equipment, testing). Worst case 2 + 1 + 2 + 2 = 7 trade asks.",
  "_sheet": "READ OFF CEO LAUNCH PLAN PACK v1 SHEET 19 (a new trade, no ratified page). Section title 'Foundry / forging, processes & capability'. Its rows are Processes, Metals, Equipment and Testing, and every row has exactly one question here.",
  "pack_id": "qp_foundry_forging",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_foundry_forging",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "v1 (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #11): new trade. Easy/Medium/Advanced tiers; 6-band experience; sheet-19 level ladder (Trainee/Operator/Skilled/Senior/Supervisor, mandatory); 1 separating confirm, the sheet's question verbatim, asked of skilled AND senior (the owner's standing rule: the sheet writes none for senior); supervisor by rule. Medium Q6 process, Q7 metal; Advanced Q9 equipment, Q10 testing, gated years OR rung. Deviations recorded: Q9 names the equipment, not its brand or tonnage (the sheet lists both; a tonnage chip set is a follow-up); Q11 'shift' is the shared qp_universal shift question and Q12 the shared ITI block (no per-trade row; PLC / EDM / heat-treatment precedent); no fresher items. Drafted for owner review (Prakash).",
